{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014vJa7E357vnEpDxf1z6kcP","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"AAAI conference paper review form rating scale\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"AI-Assisted Peer Review at Scale: The AAAI-26 AI Review Pilot\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2604.13940\"},{\"title\":\"AAAI 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/aaai-statistics/aaai-2025-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"AAAI-26 Review Process Update: Scale, Integrity Measures, and Pathways to Sustainability - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/review-process-update/\"},{\"title\":\"Matching Papers and Reviewers at Large Conferences\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2202.12273\"},{\"title\":\"Is Peer Review Really in Decline? Analyzing Review Quality across Venues and Time\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2601.15172\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some information about AAAI review processes, though the specific rating scale details vary by year. Here's what I found:\n\n**Rating Scale Information:**\n\nAAAI uses numerical rating scores where reviewer averages can range from values like 3.1 to 4.0, suggesting a scale that includes values between approximately 3 and 4+. The search results reference reviewer averages and scores being used to categorize papers into Accept, Reject, and other decision tiers.\n\nThe search results indicate that AAAI uses a reviewer-form structure for PC (Program Committee), SPC (Senior Program Committee), and AC (Area Chair) respondents, though the exact numerical scale definition isn't fully detailed in these results.\n\nFor more specific and detailed information about the exact rating scale (such as whether it's 1-5, 1-6, or another range, and what each point means), you would likely need to check:\n- The official AAAI conference website (aaai.org)\n- The submission portal or reviewer instructions for the specific year you're interested in\n- Past conference review guidelines or call for papers documentation\n\nThe rating scale may also vary slightly between different AAAI conference years.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xay766RxMufRReeFVxcA7f","session_id":"a5e85bec-84c8-44f3-af46-6eebdfb5f517","uuid":"79cfbad0-73d0-4095-939d-dbd617605193","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:54:01.225Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014MLwcNVh5vfbdxHLc75waz","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"AAAI 2026 reviewer guidelines scoring criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Main Technical Track: Call for Papers - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/main-technical-track-call/\"},{\"title\":\"AAAI 2026 First-Round Results: High Scores Rejected, AI Reviews Useful? | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/154/aaai-2026-first-round-results-high-scores-rejected-ai-reviews-useful\"},{\"title\":\"Ethical Guidelines for AAAI-26 Reviewers - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/ethical-guidelines-for-aaai-26-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for AAAI-26 Reviewers - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/instructions-for-aaai-26-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"AAAI-26 Review Process - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/review-process/\"},{\"title\":\"Call for Papers (AAAI Track) | AAMAS\",\"url\":\"https://cyprusconferences.org/aamas2026/call-for-papers-aaai-track/\"},{\"title\":\"Overview of the AI Review System\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/FAQ-for-the-AI-Assisted-Peer-Review-Process-Pilot-Program.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"AAAI-26 Review Process Update: Scale, Integrity Measures, and Pathways to Sustainability - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/review-process-update/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding AAAI 2026 reviewer guidelines and scoring criteria:\n\n## Evaluation Criteria\n\nAll submissions will be evaluated and scored for the significance and novelty of the contributions (research problems or questions addressed, methods, experiments, analyses), theoretical and/or empirical soundness of the claims, their relevance to the AAAI community, and clarity of exposition.\n\n## Types of Acceptable Contributions\n\nThe contributions may be theoretical, methodological, algorithmic, empirical, integrative (connecting ideas and methods across disparate subfields of AI), or critical (e.g., principled analyses and arguments that draw attention to problematic choice of goals, assumptions, or approaches).\n\n## Reviewer Ethical Guidelines\n\nReviewers are expected to be fair, unbiased, and objective in their evaluation of submissions and to treat all authors with respect while providing constructive feedback in a professional and courteous manner. Reviews should be depersonalized as much as possible, using terms like \"the paper\", \"the work\", \"the project\", and should focus on the work and not the individuals.\n\n## Review Process Structure\n\nEvery paper will be allocated three reviewers. AAAI-26 follows a two-phase reviewing process with two additions: an additional AI-generated review in Phase 1, and an AI-generated summary of the discussions at the end of the discussion phase.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xay766RxMufRReeFVxcA7f","session_id":"a5e85bec-84c8-44f3-af46-6eebdfb5f517","uuid":"829b8ee6-6a86-4600-aa5f-86b59f5b5828","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:54:08.867Z"}
