{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019UfbtsKxVgg9fxPrmV7761","type":"tool_result","content":"# AAAI-26 Reviewer Rating Scale and Criteria\n\nThe document provided does not specify a numerical rating scale, what individual scores mean, or list explicit evaluation criteria with defined ratings.\n\nHowever, the instructions do outline key assessment areas reviewers should address:\n\n**Main Evaluation Dimensions:**\n\n- **Problem clarity**: \"What is the problem that the paper aims to address?\"\n- **Technical soundness**: \"Is the technical approach sound and clearly described?\"\n- **Novelty and contribution**: \"What is the key novel technical contribution in the paper?\"\n- **Empirical validation**: \"Do the empirical results really support the claims of the paper?\"\n- **Reproducibility**: \"Is it expressed in sufficient detail to permit reproduction of the work?\"\n- **Related work context**: Appropriate placement within existing scholarship\n- **Evaluation quality**: Appropriate baselines, metrics, benchmarks, and error analysis\n\nThe guidelines emphasize that reviewers should frame feedback constructively: \"Instead of 'What is wrong with this paper?', ask yourself 'How could this paper be better?'\"\n\nFor the specific numerical scale and score definitions, you would need to consult the actual review submission platform or additional AAAI-26 documentation not included in this webpage content."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xay766RxMufRReeFVxcA7f","session_id":"a5e85bec-84c8-44f3-af46-6eebdfb5f517","uuid":"304456c2-1527-4e1c-be5f-bc0414a2f967","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:54:17.136Z"}
