{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EvLHuZNKTGX1r5iop4Bnp7","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"AAAI\" \"strong accept\" \"weak accept\" \"weak reject\" rating scale\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"The AI Imperative: Scaling High-Quality Peer Review in Machine Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2506.08134v1\"},{\"title\":\"Uncertainty in Artificial Intelligence\",\"url\":\"https://www.auai.org/uai2022/reviewing_instructions\"},{\"title\":\"Ucsd\",\"url\":\"https://cseweb.ucsd.edu/~jmcauley/reviews/aaai17.txt\"},{\"title\":\"Endoscopists' Acceptance on the Implementation of Artificial Intelligence in Gastrointestinal Endoscopy: Development and Case Analysis of a Scale\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9040450/\"},{\"title\":\"ICML acceptance statistics – Machine Learning (Theory)\",\"url\":\"https://hunch.net/?p=2517\"},{\"title\":\"Impact of quality of evidence on the strength of recommendations: an empirical study\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC2722589/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about the rating scale used in academic conference peer review. The AAAI rating scale includes: 10 Strong Accept (technically flawless paper with groundbreaking impact), 9 Accept (technically solid paper with high impact), 8 Weak Accept (technically sound and reasonably well-evaluated but not outstanding), 7 Borderline Accept (reasons to accept slightly outweigh reasons to reject), 6 Weak Reject (reasons to reject slightly outweigh reasons to accept), and 5 Reject (paper has clear weaknesses).\n\nThis rating scale is commonly used across machine learning and artificial intelligence conferences for evaluating submitted papers during the peer review process.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xay766RxMufRReeFVxcA7f","session_id":"a5e85bec-84c8-44f3-af46-6eebdfb5f517","uuid":"5b635b12-a720-40dd-83f2-c4f4935bcc77","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:54:34.849Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JUpHN4LzTLsoMjsNwrpZMa","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"AAAI review rating scale 1-10 accept reject borderline\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"AAAI 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/aaai-statistics/aaai-2025-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"AAAI 2026 First-Round Results: High Scores Rejected, AI Reviews Useful? | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/154/aaai-2026-first-round-results-high-scores-rejected-ai-reviews-useful\"},{\"title\":\"Allocate Marginal Reviews to Borderline Papers Using LLM Comparative Ranking\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2602.06078\"},{\"title\":\"Are reviewers suggested by authors as good as those chosen by editors? Results of a rater-blinded, retrospective study\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC1482713/\"},{\"title\":\"Matching Papers and Reviewers at Large Conferences\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2202.12273\"},{\"title\":\"A System-Level Analysis of Conference Peer Review\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2303.09020\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some relevant information about AAAI review ratings:\n\nBorderline papers are sometimes indicated with \"3 (BL)\" notation, suggesting that a score of 3 may be considered borderline. Additionally, the search results reference high review scores (ranging from 5 to 8 on what appears to be a numerical scale) being used to evaluate papers at AAAI.\n\nHowever, the search results don't provide a complete and explicit definition of the official AAAI 1-10 rating scale with specific labels for accept, reject, and borderline thresholds. The results show that AAAI uses numerical scores and references to acceptance/rejection decisions, but a comprehensive breakdown of the exact scale definitions doesn't appear in these results.\n\nIf you need more specific information about the official AAAI review rating scale definitions, you may want to check the AAAI conference's official reviewer guidelines or submission portal directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xay766RxMufRReeFVxcA7f","session_id":"a5e85bec-84c8-44f3-af46-6eebdfb5f517","uuid":"4c15c21c-85fc-4a8a-b381-2d8501d3238f","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:54:35.942Z"}
