{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012DyhURBtKTHxZy9kZrwvwY","type":"tool_result","content":"# Review Rating Scales\n\nBased on the content provided, here are the numerical rating scales used:\n\n## AAAI Scale\n**Summary Ratings:** 1-3+ scale\n- **3 (+++)**: Substantial, novel contribution; correct and clear\n- **1 (+ weak accept)**: Modest/incremental contribution\n\n## NIPS Scale\n**Multi-dimensional ratings:** 1-3 scale for each criterion\n- **3-Poster level**: \"Top 30% submissions\" or \"some notable novel contributions\" or \"good enough\"\n- **2-Sub-standard for NIPS**: Below acceptable threshold\n- **1**: (Lowest, rarely used in provided reviews)\n\n## ICML Scale\n**Overall Rating:** Ordinal scale\n- **Weak accept**: Borderline positive recommendation\n- **Weak reject**: Borderline negative recommendation\n\n**Significance ratings:**\n- **Above Average**: Interesting contributions following established work\n- **Below Average**: Incremental or insufficiently novel\n\nThe reviews emphasize that **lower NIPS scores (2) indicate weakness**, while **3s represent acceptable poster-level work**. AAAI uses direct numbering where **3 is strong acceptance** and **1 is weak acceptance**. ICML employs qualitative accept/reject language rather than numerical scores."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xay766RxMufRReeFVxcA7f","session_id":"a5e85bec-84c8-44f3-af46-6eebdfb5f517","uuid":"ba213982-d1b4-429e-b3bb-68646cbdbb05","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:54:43.525Z"}
