{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Us7yVwpxRiPFeHCFXmnazU","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"AAAI 2025 2026 review form score 5 6 7 8 9 10 rating criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"AAAI 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/aaai-statistics/aaai-2025-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"🎉 AAAI 2026 Review Results & Rebuttal Phase — What You Need to Know! | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/168/aaai-2026-review-results-rebuttal-phase-what-you-need-to-know\"},{\"title\":\"AAAI Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/aaai-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for AAAI-26 Reviewers - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/instructions-for-aaai-26-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"Thank you to our 2025 reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12905618/\"},{\"title\":\"AAAI-26 Review Process Update: Scale, Integrity Measures, and Pathways to Sustainability - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/review-process-update/\"},{\"title\":\"Thank you to our 2025 reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12853355/\"},{\"title\":\"Thank you to our 2025 reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12921489/\"},{\"title\":\"Thanks to reviewers list 2025\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12795292/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some information about AAAI review scores, but not the complete detailed rating criteria you're looking for. Here's what I found:\n\nFor AAAI 2026, most papers fall within the 5.0 to 5.8 range representing the \"upper-middle\" zone, with low-score papers (below 4.5) being rare, and some standout submissions scoring above 6.\n\nThe search results mention that reviews use numerical scores, but they don't provide the complete breakdown of what each specific score (5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10) means in terms of rating criteria. \n\nTo find the official AAAI review form with detailed scoring criteria and definitions for each rating level, I recommend:\n1. Checking the official AAAI conference website directly\n2. Looking for the reviewer guidelines on the AAAI submission system\n3. Contacting the AAAI program committee or organizing team\n\nThe search results reference \"a two-phase reviewing process\" for AAAI-26, but the specific rating definitions aren't included in the publicly available information I found.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xay766RxMufRReeFVxcA7f","session_id":"a5e85bec-84c8-44f3-af46-6eebdfb5f517","uuid":"4af72336-34f2-4a28-bf02-b5b6114a29b3","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:54:54.313Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0122AbSWj83cpPd2LNjtoJ2y","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"site:aaai.org reviewer instructions rating scale numerical\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Instructions for AAAI-26 Reviewers - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/instructions-for-aaai-26-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"Review Process - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/aaai-24-conference/review-process/\"},{\"title\":\"AAAI Launches AI-Powered Peer Review Assessment System - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/aaai-launches-ai-powered-peer-review-assessment-system/\"},{\"title\":\"How to Calibrate the Scores of Biased Reviewers by Quadratic Programming | Proceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence\",\"url\":\"https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/AAAI/article/view/7847\"},{\"title\":\"AAAI-25 Review Process - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-25/review-process/\"},{\"title\":\"AAAI-26 Review Process Update: Scale, Integrity Measures, and Pathways to Sustainability - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/review-process-update/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about AAAI reviewer instructions. The first search result links to the \"Instructions for AAAI-26 Reviewers\" page, which contains guidance on how to write professional reviews. However, the search results provided don't include detailed information about a specific numerical rating scale used in the reviewer instructions.\n\nThe results show that:\n\n- Reviewers should avoid using \"I\", \"you\", \"the authors,\" and should use depersonalized terms like \"the paper\", \"the work\", \"the project\" in their reviews\n- AAAI has specified that LLM-generated content will not provide numerical scores or ratings for papers\n\nTo get the specific details about the numerical rating scale used by human reviewers, you would need to visit the full AAAI-26 Reviewers Instructions page directly at https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/instructions-for-aaai-26-reviewers/, as the search results provided don't contain the complete rating scale information.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xay766RxMufRReeFVxcA7f","session_id":"a5e85bec-84c8-44f3-af46-6eebdfb5f517","uuid":"3905595d-32d4-486b-bfdb-c69e99f45fd1","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:54:57.001Z"}
