{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EFsjrYYrSLK3xoCjBnVSfg","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"AAAI\" review example \"overall recommendation\" score 5 6 7 8\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"An insider’s guide to author responses | Turing's Invisible Hand\",\"url\":\"https://agtb.wordpress.com/2012/03/31/an-insiders-guide-to-author-responses/\"},{\"title\":\"Overview of the AI Review System\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/FAQ-for-the-AI-Assisted-Peer-Review-Process-Pilot-Program.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Can artificial intelligence generate scientific discussion that passes peer review for publication in a high-impact orthopaedic journal?\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12413406/\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for AAAI-26 Reviewers - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/instructions-for-aaai-26-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"Matching Papers and Reviewers at Large Conferences\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2202.12273\"},{\"title\":\"Mathematical Modeling of Competitive Group Recommendation Systems with   Application to Peer Review Systems\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1204.1832\"},{\"title\":\"Automatically generating music marketplace editorial content\",\"url\":\"https://image-ppubs.uspto.gov/dirsearch-public/print/downloadPdf/8843500\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some relevant information about AAAI review scores:\n\nIn AAAI/IJCAI, an overall score of 5 is considered just below borderline, similar to a score of 6 in other conferences.\n\nThe search results also indicate that in AAAI's current reviewing system, only human reviews include paper ratings and recommendations — AI-generated reviews do not have any ratings or recommendations.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain a complete example review showing all the specific scores (5, 6, 7, 8) and how they're used in an actual AAAI review. The results reference the scoring system but don't provide a full sample review document with those specific recommendation score levels demonstrated.\n\nIf you're looking for more detailed examples of AAAI review templates or scoring rubrics, you might want to check the official AAAI conference guidelines or reviewer instructions directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xay766RxMufRReeFVxcA7f","session_id":"a5e85bec-84c8-44f3-af46-6eebdfb5f517","uuid":"e90ec4a8-5c13-4fa3-a8b2-a1d9c5942fc0","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:55:07.086Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KpNnBDqDs1ZEJuXY3PSQkH","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"AAAI 2024 2025 review form template numerical scores\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"FAQ: Reviewing – AAMAS 2025 Detroit\",\"url\":\"https://aamas2025.org/index.php/conference/frequently-asked-questions/faq-reviewing/\"},{\"title\":\"AAAI 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/aaai-statistics/aaai-2025-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"Are numerical scores important for grant assessment? A cross-sectional study\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11362741/\"},{\"title\":\"NeurIPS Fast Track Submissions - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/aaai-24-conference/neurips-fast-track-submissions/\"},{\"title\":\"Designing large language model prompts to extract scores from messy text: A shared dataset and challenge\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2601.18271\"},{\"title\":\"Large language models for abstract screening in systematic- and scoping reviews: A diagnostic test accuracy study\",\"url\":\"https://www.medrxiv.org/content/10.1101/2024.10.01.24314702.full.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Review Process - AAAI\",\"url\":\"https://aaai.org/aaai-24-conference/review-process/\"},{\"title\":\"AAAI 2024 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/aaai-paper-list/aaai-2024-paper-list/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some information about AAAI review processes and numerical scores, though the results don't contain a specific review form template document:\n\nFor AAAI-24, average score was calculated by summing scores of all reviews that gave a numerical score (potentially including meta-reviews) and dividing by the number of such reviews (not confidence-weighting).\n\nThe search results also reference reviewer averages used in the Accept tier at AAAI 2025, with scores ranging from 3.1 to 4.0, suggesting a numerical scoring scale is in use.\n\nAdditionally, related guidance from AAMAS 2025 indicates that numerical scores should never be mentioned in metareview comments, as scores are considered an imperfect reflection of review content, and decisions should instead be justified in terms of the content of the reviews.\n\nHowever, I was unable to locate the actual review form template document itself in the search results. For the specific numerical scoring scale and detailed template information for AAAI 2024/2025, you may want to check the official AAAI conference website or contact the conference organizers directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xay766RxMufRReeFVxcA7f","session_id":"a5e85bec-84c8-44f3-af46-6eebdfb5f517","uuid":"1f56d263-e00f-497f-a845-6a97608319d5","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:55:10.452Z"}
